Implement Subscription-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Feature Gating
Objective

Implement a production-ready subscription and authorization system for the QGuard Helix Platform that securely controls access to pages, dashboards, APIs, features, modules, downloads, and capabilities based on the user's active subscription plan.

The subscription system must be enforced both on the frontend and backend. Frontend route protection alone is insufficient—every protected API and server action must validate the user's subscription before granting access.

Subscription Plans

Implement the following subscription tiers:

STARTER
BASIC
PRO
ELITE

Each tier inherits access from the previous tier unless otherwise specified.

Authentication & Subscription Verification

Each authenticated user must have:

Unique User ID
Email Address
Subscription ID
Customer ID
Subscription Plan
Subscription Status
Billing Cycle
Subscription Start Date
Subscription Expiration Date
Auto-Renew Status
Payment Provider
Payment Status

Example:

User
 ├── User ID
 ├── Email
 ├── Customer ID
 ├── Subscription ID
 ├── Plan
 ├── Status
 ├── Billing Cycle
 ├── Expires At
 ├── Auto Renew
 └── Payment Provider

Subscription validation should always be performed using the authenticated user's account rather than relying solely on client-side state.

Subscription Status

Support the following states:

Active
Trial
Pending Payment
Grace Period
Past Due
Suspended
Cancelled
Expired

Only Active subscriptions should unlock protected features.

Grace Period behavior should be configurable.

Access Control Model

Implement role-based subscription authorization.

Starter
     │
     ▼
Basic
     │
     ▼
Pro
     │
     ▼
Elite

Each higher tier inherits the permissions of lower tiers.

Users Without an Active Subscription

If a user has no active subscription:

Prevent access to all dashboards
Prevent access to all platform modules
Prevent access to all APIs
Prevent access to protected downloads
Redirect protected routes to the Pricing page
Display an "Upgrade Required" screen with a call-to-action to subscribe

No premium functionality should be accessible until a valid subscription has been verified.

