Security Requirements

Implement enterprise-grade security controls:

Server-side authorization
JWT/session validation
Secure subscription verification
Protected download endpoints
API permission checks
Audit logging for authorization decisions
Graceful handling of expired subscriptions

Users must never be able to bypass feature restrictions by manipulating frontend code or API requests.

Success Criteria

The implementation is complete only when:

✅ Users without an active subscription cannot access protected pages, modules, APIs, or downloads.
✅ STARTER users can access only the QGuard Messaging dashboard and messaging-related downloads.
✅ BASIC users can access STARTER features plus the Quantum Readiness & Assessment Engine, Migration Planner, and Migration Sandbox.
✅ PRO users inherit STARTER and BASIC access and additionally gain access to Discovery, Operations, Ecosystem & Supply Chain, Intelligence, PQAuth, Observability, and Trust Center.
✅ ELITE users have unrestricted access to all current and future platform modules.
✅ Every protected frontend route and backend API enforces subscription validation.
✅ The permission system is centralized, extensible, maintainable, and production-ready.
✅ The solution is secure, scalable, and suitable for enterprise customer deployment.